  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14219884/assets/f52592db0fee86e26318d6d2de9d7f685f1fb9f5d416628a04878857f1c54b54.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14219884/assets/76f0da764caf0237a2d30d32d593886d8df6c348368fe889f7447be781b6faf1.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14219884/assets/9778abd955cdc9b705800eba8f3d0d635af1c6a5fd5724583bdb32a943c6d44f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-155031\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.</p>\n<p>With that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Diagram I shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-155031-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-155031-e-0\"></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Diagram II shows three points that are <em>not</em> collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-155031-e-1\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-155031-e-1\"></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Diagram III shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-155031-e-2\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-155031-e-2\"></div>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"</p>\n</div>",
